usage: flow fir-g [-h] [--json] [--device {cpu,numpy,mlx,auto}] [--bench]
                  [--calibrate] [--thresholds THRESHOLDS] [--opts]
                  [--apply PASSES] [program]

Flow FIR-G: program graph + CPU/MLX analyses

positional arguments:
  program               .flow source file (optional with --calibrate alone)

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --json                machine-readable report
  --device {cpu,numpy,mlx,auto}
                        analysis device (default: cpu). auto uses measured
                        thresholds (uncalibrated → cpu)
  --bench               print rough CPU vs bulk wall times for this program
  --calibrate           sweep synthetic graph sizes, measure break-even, save
                        thresholds
  --thresholds THRESHOLDS
                        path to fir_g_route.json (default:
                        $FLOW_FIR_G_THRESHOLDS or
                        ~/.cache/flow/fir_g_route.json)
  --opts                list deterministic optimisation candidates (dead_elim
                        / inline)
  --apply PASSES        apply optimisation passes and report the rewritten
                        graph. PASSES is a comma list from
                        {dead_elim, const_fold, dce, all}.
                        With --opts, candidates reflect the post-pass graph
